            <title>[LU-20539] changed.py: unchanged subtests marked as changed</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20539</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;changed.py will mark a subtest as changed when the diff context specifies a test and non-test functions are subsequently changed. For example:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
diff --git a/lustre/tests/conf-sanity.sh b/lustre/tests/conf-sanity.sh
index 5f6483d8f1..c7f7138fec 100644
--- a/lustre/tests/conf-sanity.sh
+++ b/lustre/tests/conf-sanity.sh
@@ -10157,6 +10157,169 @@ test_153a() {
&#160;}
&#160;run_test 153a &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;bypass invalid NIDs quickly&quot;&lt;/span&gt;

+cleanup_200() {
+ local modopts=$1
+ stopall -f
+ MODOPTS_LIBCFS=$modopts
+ load_modules_local libcfs
+}
+ &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
